{"event_type":"review","id":"9c4c924c9f218be06885fdfa007b15a80031f17b9aefb42097bed2772bc4b146","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T21:50:49Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3a7c045319d443eb8bc1de83dee7df1edc03111450cbe67b3f952588c9e46738","sha256":"3a7c045319d443eb8bc1de83dee7df1edc03111450cbe67b3f952588c9e46738"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/478f94072c6de01d5de9da830a935b677693cc9f2a00c54fa0ab9a10d5357022","sha256":"478f94072c6de01d5de9da830a935b677693cc9f2a00c54fa0ab9a10d5357022"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/fc391f862b470a35bff454832f4ee2b726e618691d2bc8f7e4154a4ad361402a","sha256":"fc391f862b470a35bff454832f4ee2b726e618691d2bc8f7e4154a4ad361402a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/85bfd8203905f0c31a40d4445df3aee48422d1dbdfc794082cbed3ae75ccb6ec","sha256":"85bfd8203905f0c31a40d4445df3aee48422d1dbdfc794082cbed3ae75ccb6ec"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/21fd480fe9af30209af49fab691428c4e2e5be81a6a10f9e87c29781288b1e72","sha256":"21fd480fe9af30209af49fab691428c4e2e5be81a6a10f9e87c29781288b1e72"}],"attempt_id":"a5ddeba83d9f4f53ebdc596bfcff38ab766b3031602adabcc91100bab5852236:0:1","base":"04a998790f8e1ac7f41a28b986a491a4aa54baea","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"9eea32ef3b619ad5c434da00abb08195cb30c8b3","body":"**Timeout or abort can overwrite a completed exit as `killed`.**\n\n`close` waits for both pipes to close. If the shell exits normally but a backgrounded descendant keeps stdout or stderr open (`cmd &`), `close` is delayed. A timeout or abort in that window sets `killedByUs`. Line 128 then settles `killed` and drops the real exit code, even though the command had already finished.\n\nRecord the exit code at the `exit` event, but only when `killedByUs` is still false at that moment. Then prefer that code in `close`.\n\nA separate effect applies when `timeoutMs` is `undefined`. The same backgrounded-descendant case never settles, because only the timer or an abort can force `close`. If that is unintended, add a bounded grace after `exit` before settling.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     let spawnError: unknown;\n+    let exitedCleanly: number | undefined;\n+    child.on('exit', (code: number | null, signal: NodeJS.Signals | null) => {\n+      if (!killedByUs && signal === null && code !== null) exitedCleanly = code;\n+    });\n     child.on('error', (e: unknown) => {\n       spawnError ??= e;\n     });\n@@\n-      } else if (killedByUs || signal !== null || code === null) {\n+      } else if (exitedCleanly === undefined && (killedByUs || signal !== null || code === null)) {\n         settle({ kind: 'killed', stdout, stderr, overflowed });\n       } else {\n-        settle({ kind: 'exit', code, stdout, stderr, overflowed });\n+        settle({ kind: 'exit', code: exitedCleanly ?? code!, stdout, stderr, overflowed });\n       }\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 120-132","id":"1c6c5fb8e640872b3b425bba53ce0dee09f39782e33307ed589fcc1b9d8df125","intervals":[[92,92]],"path":"src/harness/run.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Timeout or abort can overwrite a completed exit as `killed`."}],"head":"6df9b1fe5e13565176fbf8351c15364790d3f59a","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"175498e9b36ac6c25c5994d163956309c5d14b13","intervals":[[1,42]],"path":"src/harness/failures.ts"},{"blob":"9eea32ef3b619ad5c434da00abb08195cb30c8b3","intervals":[[1,135]],"path":"src/harness/run.ts"},{"blob":"6cd11be1c9fcc79e392b5271fe36e35730326c92","intervals":[[1,457]],"path":"src/harness/surface.ts"}],"job_id":"a5ddeba83d9f4f53ebdc596bfcff38ab766b3031602adabcc91100bab5852236:0","outcome":"completed","paths":